Use of Switch: 8/10 — Switch rooms connect the agents and team workflow, though the write-up leaves some integration details and model-provider setup marked planned.

Technical execution: 7/10 — The repo layout and run instructions are detailed, and a real PR loop is claimed; the optional Docker stack is unrun, and I can’t verify the claims from code or video.

Creativity and impact: 8/10 — Testing team-defined business rules with exploits and regression checks addresses a real gap in conventional security scanning.

Presentation and documentation: 7/10 — The README explains the workflow and architecture well, but no demo video is included here and some status claims conflict.

Shortlist: Yes — The idea and claimed end-to-end PR loop merit a closer look, with implementation and demo verification still needed.

Three biggest weaknesses:
1. The submission’s status is inconsistent: it says the full loop is verified, but also marks model providers planned.
2. Reproduction is less clear for the core agent workflow than for the landing page and wallet API.
3. The demo video is unavailable in the provided material, limiting presentation assessment.

TOTAL: 7.6
